    <ObjectList>
      <MultilingualText ID="1" CompositionName="Comment">
        <ObjectList>
          <MultilingualTextItem ID="2" CompositionName="Items">
            <AttributeList>
              <Culture>en-US</Culture>
              <Text>Supervises the shredder hopper high-level sensor: raises a latched hopper-blockage alarm (and a stop/inhibit demand) when the hopper stays (debounced-)high for a cumulative threshold of time while the plant is running, i.e. the shredder/pusher is not clearing it (S6 request #1, REQ-HBA-001..007). Purely supervisory - it commands no motion and writes no shared tag; the alarm and the stop demand are exposed on its own IO interface and wired to annunciation / the actual stop at a separate integration step (Q-HBA-05). Cumulative timing is pause-and-resume (NEW-HBA-01): losing PlantRunning freezes the elapsed and resumes, so 60 s of blockage need not be contiguous. Built from a plain TON, never TONR (C-406), plus a banked up-accumulator compared against the threshold (see NETWORK 3-4). The alarm latch lives in the RETAIN interface and deliberately survives a power cycle (C-124 carve-out, NEW-HBA-04) - like the sequencer's DischargeConveyorTimeoutFault, a blockage needing a human still needs FaultReset after a restart; all transient timing state is non-retentive and self-clears at startup (NEW-HBA-06, no OB100 edit). Tunables BlockedTimeThreshold (T#60S) and ClearDebounceTime (T#2S) are this instance's own settings (C-307), not shared DB members.</Text>
            </AttributeList>
          </MultilingualTextItem>
        </ObjectList>
      </MultilingualText>
