          <MultilingualText ID="E" CompositionName="Comment">
            <ObjectList>
              <MultilingualTextItem ID="F" CompositionName="Items">
                <AttributeList>
                  <Culture>en-US</Culture>
                  <Text>Banks cumulative high-and-running time across plant-stop pauses (NEW-HBA-01). AccumulatedElapsed has two writers that can never fire in the same scan: it goes back to T#0S once the hopper is no longer qualified high (a confirmed clear), and it is otherwise banked up by the just-ended segment's elapsed when the plant stops with the hopper still blocked. An operator FaultReset appears nowhere here: acknowledging an alarm says nothing about the hopper, so it neither discards nor freezes the accumulated evidence (REQ-HBA-005). PauseEdge is the falling edge of BlockActive, taken against the previous-scan copy that the coil below it then updates - the two coils must stay in this order or the edge never fires. Both PauseEdge and the bank read PersistenceTimer.ET before NETWORK 4 re-evaluates the timer this scan, so the elapsed banked is the just-completed segment's, with no separate held-value register needed.</Text>
                </AttributeList>
              </MultilingualTextItem>
            </ObjectList>
          </MultilingualText>
