                <AttributeList>
                  <Culture>en-US</Culture>
                  <Text>Times the current contiguous high-and-running segment, and adds the banked pause time to it: CumulativeElapsed is the total cumulative high-and-running time that NETWORK 5 compares against BlockedTimeThreshold. The timer runs on the blockage-and-running condition alone - an operator FaultReset does not stop, freeze or rewind the segment in progress (REQ-HBA-005). PT is BlockedTimeThreshold only so that a single uninterrupted segment can itself reach the threshold; the trip is the comparison in NETWORK 5, never the timer's own Q.</Text>
