        <ObjectList>
          <MultilingualText ID="18" CompositionName="Comment">
            <ObjectList>
              <MultilingualTextItem ID="19" CompositionName="Items">
                <AttributeList>
                  <Culture>en-US</Culture>
                  <Text>Latches the hopper-blockage alarm when the cumulative high-and-running time reaches BlockedTimeThreshold, and holds it until an operator acknowledges. The acknowledgement is the moment FaultReset goes true, not the fact that it is true: a reset left on, wired on or stuck on clears the latch once and cannot hold the alarm off afterwards (REQ-HBA-005). Because the reset leaves the accumulated evidence alone, the latch re-evaluates on the very next scan against that same evidence - a hopper still blocked past the threshold re-alarms at once, whether or not the plant is running, while a hopper whose evidence has been discarded stays quiet. The reset pulse is taken against the previous-scan copy that the coil below it then updates - the two coils must stay in this order or the pulse never fires. The latch lives in the RETAIN interface and survives a power cycle: a blockage that needed a human still needs acknowledging after a restart, and the stop demand below stays asserted until it gets one.</Text>
                </AttributeList>
              </MultilingualTextItem>
            </ObjectList>
          </MultilingualText>
          <MultilingualText ID="1A" CompositionName="Title">
            <ObjectList>
              <MultilingualTextItem ID="1B" CompositionName="Items">
                <AttributeList>
                  <Culture>en-US</Culture>
                  <Text>Hopper-Blocked Alarm Latch (RETAIN - Survives Power Cycle)</Text>
                </AttributeList>
              </MultilingualTextItem>
            </ObjectList>
          </MultilingualText>
        </ObjectList>
